  {
   "topic": "Two ratings per voltage",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Every voltage is characterised for regulation: Zener voltage window, reverse leakage and dynamic resistance at the test current IZT1, with VZ read under a pulse of at most 5 ms. The 7.5 V to 200 V parts are also characterised for transient protection, with leakage at a working voltage and a maximum clamping voltage at a rated 10/1000 µs surge current."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Surge pulse definition",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "The 10/1000 µs surge current pulse has a front time t1 = 10 µs to its peak IRSM (100 %), with the front marked at its 10 % and 90 % levels, and an exponential tail that is down to 50 % of peak at t2 = 1000 µs."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Dissipation and derating",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "With the lead held at temperature (RthJL = 30 K/W) the diode carries 2.3 W up to 105 °C, falling linearly to zero at 175 °C. Mounted on 3 mm x 3 mm pads (RthJA = 180 K/W) it carries 0.8 W up to 30 °C ambient, falling linearly to zero at 175 °C."
  },
